      "problem": "Rewrite the statement $¬((¬X∨Y)∧(¬Y∨X))$ using De Morgan's laws.",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's laws state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(X∧Y)≡¬X∨¬Y, \\\\ ¬(X∨Y)≡¬X∧¬Y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can simplify the given statement as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬((¬X∨Y)∧(¬Y∨X)) & ≡¬(¬X∨Y)∨¬(¬Y∨X) \\\\  & ≡(¬(¬X)∧¬Y)∨(¬(¬Y)∧¬X) \\\\  & ≡(X∧¬Y)∨(Y∧¬X)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
